-->\n    <rect x=\"264\" y=\"170\" width=\"26\" height=\"140\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <rect x=\"294\" y=\"289\" width=\"14\" height=\"21\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n    <text x=\"277\" y=\"164\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"8.5\" fill=\"#1e3a8a\">175K<\/text>\n    <text x=\"277\" y=\"324\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#5b6b7f\">7/22<\/text>\n    <!-- 6 9/2/22 125,000 / 18,750 -->\n    <rect x=\"322\" y=\"210\" width=\"26\" height=\"100\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <rect x=\"352\" y=\"295\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n    <text x=\"335\" y=\"204\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"8.5\" fill=\"#1e3a8a\">125K<\/text>\n    <text x=\"335\" y=\"324\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#5b6b7f\">9/2<\/text>\n    <!-- 7 10/31/22 198,000 / 29,700 -->\n    <rect x=\"380\" y=\"151.6\" width=\"26\" height=\"158.4\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <rect x=\"410\" y=\"286.2\" width=\"14\" height=\"23.8\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n    <text x=\"393\" y=\"145\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"8.5\" fill=\"#1e3a8a\">198K<\/text>\n    <text x=\"393\" y=\"324\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#5b6b7f\">10/31<\/text>\n    <!-- 8 12/15/22 167,000 / 25,050 -->\n    <rect x=\"438\" y=\"176.4\" width=\"26\" height=\"133.6\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <rect x=\"468\" y=\"290\" width=\"14\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n    <text x=\"451\" y=\"170\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"8.5\" fill=\"#1e3a8a\">167K<\/text>\n    <text x=\"451\" y=\"324\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#5b6b7f\">12/15<\/text>\n    <!-- 9 2/17/23 210,000 / 31,500 -->\n    <rect x=\"496\" y=\"142\" width=\"26\" height=\"168\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <rect x=\"526\" y=\"284.8\" width=\"14\" height=\"25.2\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n    <text x=\"509\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"8.5\" fill=\"#1e3a8a\">210K<\/text>\n    <text x=\"509\" y=\"324\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#5b6b7f\">2/17<\/text>\n    <!-- 10 3/27/23 185,000 / 27,750 -->\n    <rect x=\"554\" y=\"162\" width=\"26\" height=\"148\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <rect x=\"584\" y=\"287.8\" width=\"14\" height=\"22.2\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n    <text x=\"567\" y=\"156\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"8.5\" fill=\"#1e3a8a\">185K<\/text>\n    <text x=\"567\" y=\"324\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#5b6b7f\">3/27<\/text>\n    <!-- 11 4/14/23 64,000 / 9,600  OFF-LEDGER -->\n    <rect x=\"612\" y=\"258.8\" width=\"26\" height=\"51.2\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/>\n    <rect x=\"642\" y=\"302.3\" width=\"14\" height=\"7.7\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n    <text x=\"625\" y=\"252\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"8.5\" fill=\"#991b1b\">64K*<\/text>\n    <text x=\"625\" y=\"324\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#991b1b\">4/14*<\/text>\n    <!-- 12 5/8/23 245,000 / 36,750 -->\n    <rect x=\"670\" y=\"114\" width=\"26\" height=\"196\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <rect x=\"700\" y=\"280.6\" width=\"14\" height=\"29.4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n    <text x=\"683\" y=\"108\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"8.5\" fill=\"#1e3a8a\">245K<\/text>\n    <text x=\"683\" y=\"324\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#5b6b7f\">5/8<\/text>\n    <!-- 13 6/19/23 195,000 / 29,250 -->\n    <rect x=\"728\" y=\"154\" width=\"26\" height=\"156\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <rect x=\"758\" y=\"286.6\" width=\"14\" height=\"23.4\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n    <text x=\"741\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"8.5\" fill=\"#1e3a8a\">195K<\/text>\n    <text x=\"741\" y=\"324\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#5b6b7f\">6/19<\/text>\n    <!-- 14 8/21/23 275,000 / 41,250 -->\n    <rect x=\"786\" y=\"90\" width=\"26\" height=\"220\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <rect x=\"816\" y=\"277\" width=\"14\" height=\"33\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n    <text x=\"799\" y=\"84\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"8.5\" fill=\"#1e3a8a\">275K<\/text>\n    <text x=\"799\" y=\"324\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"9\" fill=\"#5b6b7f\">8/21<\/text>\n    <!-- legend -->\n    <rect x=\"620\" y=\"24\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/>\n    <text x=\"640\" y=\"35\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#26313f\">DataPulse → Cerulean payment (Mar 2022–Aug 2023; total $2,213,000)<\/text>\n    <rect x=\"620\" y=\"44\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/>\n    <text x=\"640\" y=\"55\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#26313f\">off-ledger payment, no AP entry (*; $48,000 + $64,000 = $112,000)<\/text>\n    <rect x=\"620\" y=\"64\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#f59e0b\"/>\n    <text x=\"640\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"10.5\" fill=\"#26313f\">Cerulean → \"M. Ridley\" personal acct, exactly 15% of its paired payment (Σ $331,950; lag 5–8 business days)<\/text>\n  <\/g>\n<\/svg>\n<figcaption><b>Figure 2 — The Cerulean kickback pattern.<\/b> Each amber bar is exactly 15% of its\npaired payment and lands in Ridley's personal account 5–8 business days later, under rotating\n\"referral fee / commission / advisory fee\" memos. This pattern — and the two off-ledger payments\nthat still received 15% transfers — is the core evidence in memo §IV.A. Values are the extracted\nfigures from <code>cerulean-transaction-records.xlsx<\/code>; bar heights are to scale\n($0.0008 px per $1,000).<\/figcaption>\n<\/figure>\n\n<h2>What happened — verification and fixes<\/h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><b>Deliverable is a real Office document.<\/b> <code>investigation-issue-memorandum.docx<\/code>\n  (≈36&nbsp;KB) is a valid OOXML package (<code>word/document.xml<\/code> present) generated with\n  <code>pandoc draft/memo.md -f markdown -t docx<\/code>. It round-trips cleanly back through pandoc\n  to plain text, so it will open without issue in the evaluator's tooling.<\/li>\n  <li><b>Machine-checked against the sources.<\/b> A check script (~60 groups of literal values — every\n  dollar figure, date, person, account suffix, wire reference, Bates range, policy threshold, and key\n  quoted phrase) was run against the round-tripped memo text. <b>All checks pass<\/b>; the single flagged\n  item was a typographic-apostrophe difference (\"shouldn't\" rendered as \"shouldn't\") that I confirmed\n  present by hand.<\/li>\n  <li><b>Arithmetic re-verified<\/b> independently: $2,101,000 + $48,000 + $64,000 = $2,213,000;\n  15% × $2,213,000 = $331,950; 3 × $62,500 = $187,500 = 37.5% of $500,000; $960,000 + $150,000 =\n  $1,110,000; $87,450 + $102,000 = $189,450; and the exposure sum\n  $2,213,000 + $1,310,000 + $1,110,000 + ≈$430,000 = ≈$4,663,000.<\/li>\n  <li><b>One fix pass came out of verification:<\/b> Pinnacle Edge success-fee invoice IDs/dates corrected\n  against the spreadsheet rows (PE-2022-009, PE-2023-004, PE-2023-008), the PT Nusantara \"14 vs 15 days\"\n  discrepancy between sources stated explicitly, and the 60% JV stake plus the named CEO and Graystone\n  lead accountant added for completeness.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<h2>What you should know<\/h2>\n<div class=\"callout warn\">\n  <b>Caveats, stated plainly:<\/b>\n  <ul>\n    <li><b>The memo date is a choice, not a fact from the sources.<\/b> The latest dated artifact in the\n    record is the Graystone report of Nov&nbsp;3, 2023; I dated the memo Nov&nbsp;15, 2023 so it sits\n    after every source document. Nothing in the sources specifies the actual date of this deliverable.<\/li>\n    <li><b>Authorship follows the sources' convention.<\/b> The engagement letter assigns the issue\n    memorandum to Whitfield &amp; Crane (lead: Sarah Delacroix), so the memo is written as that firm's\n    product to the Audit Committee — a drafting convention, not an assertion that those lawyers wrote it.<\/li>\n    <li><b>The findings are as preliminary as the sources themselves.<\/b> Ridgeview Holdings' beneficial\n    ownership is inferential pending Cayman legal process; the second and third Albion installments are\n    unconfirmed; PT Nusantara downstream payments are undetermined; the insider-trading question is open.\n    The memo says so in §X (Reservations) rather than overclaiming.<\/li>\n    <li><b>The sources contradict each other in a few places<\/b>, and the memo handles rather than hides\n    this: the JV compilation misnames two entities (\"Cerulean Policy Group\", \"Pinnacle Edge Advisory LLC\" —\n    I used the official names); the CFO interview date differs between documents (Oct 10 vs Oct 20 — not\n    stated in the memo); and the whistleblower's \"early invoices of $15,000–$25,000\" understate the actual\n    ledger, which the memo notes.<\/li>\n    <li><b>No fact was invented or imported.<\/b> Every figure, name, date, and quote in the memo traces\n    to one of the ten workspace source files (mapping in <code>process/notes-02-evidence.md<\/code>). I did\n    not perform any real-world verification; the sources were designated authoritative for this exercise.<\/li>\n  <\/ul>\n<\/div>\n\n<h3>Files left in the workspace<\/h3>\n<table class=\"kv\">\n  <tr><td>Deliverable<\/td><td><code>/app/workspace/investigation-issue-memorandum.docx<\/code> — the issue memorandum (opens with pandoc or any Office app)<\/td><\/tr>\n  <tr><td>Draft source<\/td><td><code>/app/workspace/draft/memo.md<\/code> — markdown used to build the docx<\/td><\/tr>\n  <tr><td>Session record<\/td><td><code>/app/workspace/process/<\/code> — extracted sources (<code>src-*.txt<\/code>, <code>*-xlsx.txt<\/code>, <code>email-decoded.txt<\/code>), evidence log (<code>notes-02-evidence.md<\/code>), check script (<code>verify.py<\/code>), round-trip output (<code>memo-roundtrip.txt<\/code>), and outcome notes (<code>notes-03-verification-outcome.md<\/code>)<\/td><\/tr>\n<\/table>\n\n<footer>\nSelf-contained report generated from this task session only. Figures are inline SVG authored from the\nsession's own extracted data (Figure 1: workflow diagram; Figure 2: bar plot of the Cerulean ledger and\ntransfer records). No external data, no generated imagery.\n<\/footer>\n\n<\/div>\n<\/body>\n<\/html>\n"}, "same_run": "harvey-labs--codex--white-collar-defense-investigations-identify-suspicious-patterns-in-financial-transaction-records"});
